/**
  @page guides-meshes-iteration Mesh iteration
  @brief Traverse vertices, cells, facets and incident entities.

  @tableofcontents
  @m_footernavigation

  @section guides-meshes-iteration-intro Iterator state

  A mesh iterator identifies an entity of a particular dimension. Dereference
  it while `!iterator.end()` holds, then advance with `++iterator`. Entity
  indices are local to their dimension. Topology changes can invalidate
  iterators and indices; finish traversal before rebuilding the mesh.

  @section guides-meshes-iteration-basic Select the entity family

  @subsection guides-meshes-iteration-basic-vertices Vertices

  `mesh.getVertex()` traverses vertices. The dereferenced object provides its
  physical coordinates through `getCoordinates()`.

  @subsection guides-meshes-iteration-basic-cells Cells

  `mesh.getCell()` traverses the highest-dimensional entities. The checked
  example prints each cell's optional attribute and geometric measure.

  @snippet Geometry/MeshBasics.cpp mesh-basics-iterate

  @subsection guides-meshes-iteration-basic-faces Facets

  `mesh.getFace()` traverses codimension-one facets. Compute the relevant
  connectivity first: edges must exist before a triangular mesh can report
  its complete facet set.

  @section guides-meshes-iteration-dimension Select a dimension

  `mesh.getPolytope(d)` traverses entities of dimension `d`. The same index
  value in two dimensions identifies different entities. Compute the required
  lower-dimensional entities before traversing them.

  @section guides-meshes-iteration-properties Entity properties

  @subsection guides-meshes-iteration-properties-index Index

  `iterator->getIndex()` identifies the current entity within its dimension.
  Mesh rebuilding can assign new indices.

  @subsection guides-meshes-iteration-properties-coords Coordinates

  Vertex coordinates describe mesh geometry. An interior sample is represented
  by a `Geometry::Point` on a cell; the
  @ref guides-quadrature "quadrature example" shows this distinction.

  @subsection guides-meshes-iteration-properties-attribute Attribute

  `getAttribute()` returns an optional label. Test it before dereferencing or
  using its value as a key. The source snippet above includes both operations.

  @subsection guides-meshes-iteration-properties-geometry Reference shape

  `getGeometry()` returns the `Polytope::Type` of the current entity. This
  selects the reference shape for local geometry and finite element operations.

  @section guides-meshes-iteration-specific Start at an index

  `mesh.getCell(i)`, `mesh.getFace(i)` and `mesh.getVertex(i)` return iterators
  positioned at an existing entity. Check the corresponding entity count
  before using an externally supplied index.

  @section guides-meshes-iteration-neighbors Cell neighbors

  Compute `mesh.getConnectivity().compute(d, d)` for the cell dimension `d`
  before traversing `cell->getAdjacent()`. The detailed
  @ref guides-meshes-connectivity "connectivity guide" describes incidence
  and adjacency separately.

  @section guides-meshes-iteration-boundary Boundary facets

  `mesh.getBoundary()` traverses facets with one incident cell, after
  facet-to-cell connectivity has been computed. The example counts six
  boundary segments around its rectangle.

  @section guides-meshes-iteration-interface Interior facets

  `mesh.getInterface()` traverses interior facets. For transmission problems,
  select the desired pair of region attributes before assigning interface
  labels; see @ref guides-interfaces-dg.

  @section guides-meshes-iteration-example Complete source

  @ref Geometry/MeshBasics.cpp "MeshBasics.cpp" constructs the mixed mesh,
  computes incidences, traverses cells and extracts its boundary.

  @section guides-meshes-iteration-performance Repeated traversal

  Prepare the required incidence relations once before repeated traversal.
  Retain only the quantities needed by the algorithm; coordinate evaluation
  and geometric measures may require additional geometry calculations.

  @section guides-meshes-iteration-see-also Continue

  - @ref guides-meshes-queries "Counts, measures and attributes"
  - @ref guides-meshes-utilities "Extraction and partitioning"
*/
